SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Go to the nearest Emergency Department immediately if your testicles suddenly become swollen and severely painful, if you develop a high fever, or if your knees, wrists, or ankles suddenly become swollen, red, and painful to move.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The severe pain and thick discharge are caused by an aggressive bacterial infection in your urethra. The intramuscular antibiotic injection specifically targets and rapidly kills this main bacteria, while the oral tablets ensure any hidden, secondary bacteria are also destroyed.
Actionable Steps: Do not engage in any sexual activity for a full 7 days to allow your tissues to heal and to guarantee you do not pass the infection on. Drink plenty of water to naturally flush the dead bacteria and inflammatory debris out of your urinary tract.

